' A real, ordinary ArcoBASIC program meant to be compiled BY the Fission
' Compiler Substrate's own native x86-64 backend (fission/amir/lower_x86_64.abas)
' -- see fission/tests/native_programs/hello_native.abas's own header
' comment for the directory convention.
'
' Array.Sort -- a real NEW array (the oracle's own `array_sort_function`
' copies its argument into a fresh array before sorting, never mutating
' the caller's own array), ascending order. Number-kind sorts
' numerically; String-kind sorts by ordinary byte-wise ordering (matching
' `std::string::operator<` -- uppercase letters sort before lowercase
' ones). Number and String only -- a real, disclosed, narrower remaining
' scope cut, matching the same Number-vs-String-only precedent already
' established for Array.Find/Contains/Join elsewhere in this backend.
'
' Expected output verified against legacy `ArcoFission compile-run` on this
' identical source as the equivalence-testing oracle.
nums = [5, 30, 10, 20, -5, 0]
sortedNums = Array.Sort(nums)
PRINT sortedNums
PRINT nums

strs = ["banana", "apple", "Cherry", "apple"]
sortedStrs = Array.Sort(strs)
PRINT sortedStrs
PRINT strs
